<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:08:42Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Seoul fears being sidelined as US reaches out to North Korea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93ad0e0d0e0670bba0745d4de734ce4d81a116f92584903cdf0d560293dfb885</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:08:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T14:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/seoul-fears-being-sidelined-as-us-reaches-out-to-north-korea/a-79808098--b371be6c550b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/seoul-fears-being-sidelined-as-us-reaches-out-to-north-korea/a-79808098?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With ties between South Korea and the Trump administration strained, the South Korean government worries that Donald Trump's pursuit of a diplomatic breakthrough with Kim Jong Un may come at Seoul's expense.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Bollywood and the underworld — together in the spotlight?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:34b55c55097fde049c9dc6206180084f9757448ac72afb4bb497ec8b377df875</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:08:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T14:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bollywood-and-the-underworld-together-in-the-spotlight/a-79806129--e6b957cc58ac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bollywood-and-the-underworld-together-in-the-spotlight/a-79806129?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A wave of shootings and extortion threats has rattled India's film industry. This time, those claiming responsibility are very different from the Mumbai underworld that had Bollywood in its grip back in the 1990s.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany takes cautious approach on Israeli election results</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:65d4a05de920eb585bcd21eccfda42c5968d707efdb7d6dd5585d71dcdc947c7</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:08:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T11:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-takes-cautious-approach-on-israeli-election-results/a-79805184--6eb977f23eb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-takes-cautious-approach-on-israeli-election-results/a-79805184?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German politicians have been slow to respond as they wait to see who is likely to comprise the next coalition. Many are also hoping for a government without religious hardliners.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>India increases growth forecast for fiscal year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02ed1e9ec79d1f9d4aa4771bdcb7264fc85d94c7f8c1984fe907130109f6e17a</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T16:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-increases-growth-forecast-for-fiscal-year/a-79798971--fa1e5ffdabbe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-increases-growth-forecast-for-fiscal-year/a-79798971?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">India's Ministry of Finance has increased its growth forecasts for the current fiscal year. But it also warned about inflation, particularly for fuel and energy, amid continued instability in the Middle East.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>China leaders demand more loyalty and more initiative</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b17177d009eb7aa92446b27102711071dabc9e61d8d4dc6b3d26aacd78417361</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T16:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-leaders-demand-more-loyalty-and-more-initiative/a-79799138--290c6fd05de3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-leaders-demand-more-loyalty-and-more-initiative/a-79799138?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The CCP session emphasized internal discipline, as expected, but left the question of Xi Jinping's successor unanswered. The party seems anxious of any instability as geopolitics heats up and China's economy cools down.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Human trafficking victims stranded in Guinea-Bissau</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6c04147ecd951e665dd57c764e38c2b2a6c06b817b7f0cf5df2baf80cee43c9e</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T14:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/human-trafficking-victims-stranded-in-guinea-bissau/a-79785558--af9688fcc3e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/human-trafficking-victims-stranded-in-guinea-bissau/a-79785558?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Dozens of West Africans lured to Guinea-Bissau with promises of jobs and migration to Europe say they were exploited by a suspected trafficking network. Now many cannot afford to return home.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Can EU and India work together to secure Indo-Pacific?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04537ee63c62def2c9e0e15fcb56aa17e47dd8d3b4dc5e6de3f764437d443745</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T13:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-eu-and-india-work-together-to-secure-indo-pacific/a-79796195--03242e3284fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-eu-and-india-work-together-to-secure-indo-pacific/a-79796195?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">India and Europe are deepening defense ties, but their clashing perspectives on Russia and differing priorities on China are hampering their joint ambitions on maritime security.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>European Central Bank (ECB) head Christine Lagarde to step down in February, before her term ends</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:21de815797c0727d8bc12dbb87edcbf79d7c7b3f42302c1f0b9c5372a5ab08b1</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T10:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/european-central-bank-ecb-head-christine-lagarde-to-step-down-in-february-before-her-term-ends/a-79794353--c27511a3878b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/european-central-bank-ecb-head-christine-lagarde-to-step-down-in-february-before-her-term-ends/a-79794353?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">European Central Bank (ECB) President Christine Lagarde is to resign nine months ahead of the end of her 8-year term. European Council President Antonio Costa has said the process to find a successor is underway.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ship reported on fire off Oman as Iran escalation fears mount</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bfed07dce2c75fd655e4f7f15417c4bdf6f43a772b2a807fbc0b01b6371a361d</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T10:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ship-reported-on-fire-off-oman-as-iran-escalation-fears-mount/a-79792733--778ab60c5f97.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ship-reported-on-fire-off-oman-as-iran-escalation-fears-mount/a-79792733?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A ship in the Strait of Hormuz is reported to be on fire, a British maritime agency says. Iran has meanwhile said it has shot down another US drone as military tensions with Washington continue.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Flavio Bolsonaro lands in US, declares himself 'leader' of Brazil</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a1fd404b93bd4e114e5f5897909f26fe382dfbce9e1a015f7f1ee3f473f4ee4</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T22:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/flavio-bolsonaro-lands-in-us-declares-himself-leader-of-brazil/a-79788659--e413c3c7c69a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/flavio-bolsonaro-lands-in-us-declares-himself-leader-of-brazil/a-79788659?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Flavio Bolsonaro declared himself the rightful leader of his country despite losing the presidential election runoff on Sunday. He and his family have fled to the US.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US midterms: What you need to know</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:695a40674df49780b5dd33f287c96e0e431799014a13bc09629ea8ed5ee43841</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T19:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-do-the-us-midterms-work-and-why-are-they-so-important-for-trump-s-presidency/a-79789932--5c980e8318e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-midterms-what-you-need-to-know/a-79789932?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US voters are electing a new Congress. The results will be decisive for the future of the United States, and a judgment on Donald Trump's second term as president.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
